  "note": "Century Gothic ships only inside Office (Word's DFonts), so Chromium fell to\nthe Helvetica-class sans: ~9% narrower per body line (hmtx of both fonts,\n2026-09-12). Its geometry is not a uniform scale of Liberation Sans: the\nlowercase runs +10.6% (+1.7% bold), capitals -5% (-7.3% bold), digits, space\nand punctuation within 1%, so per-case faces carry the adjustment (later\nfaces win inside their unicode-range). Latin-1 accented letters measure\nthe same per-case ratios and share the faces; Latin Extended-A does not. Pitch stays the probed 1.226\n(`lineHeightFactor`).",
